      "title": "Sydney trader sacked for working from Singapore without permission wins unfair dismissal case",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/09/sydney-currency-trader-sacked-for-working-from-singapore-without-permission-wins-unfair-dismissal-case",
      "description": "<p>Employee had also been in Bali when he told his manager he was working from home, Fair Work Commission hears</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A Sydney currency trader who was sacked for working from Singapore without approval has won an unfair dismissal case, but failed to be awarded compensation.</p><p>The Fair Work Commission ruled on Wednesday that Charles Graham had been unfairly dismissed by HIFX Australia, trading as Xe, in December last year.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/09/sydney-currency-trader-sacked-for-working-from-singapore-without-permission-wins-unfair-dismissal-case\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
