      "title": "Women with PMOS should get subsidised weight-loss drugs, Australian advocates say",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/10/women-with-pmos-should-get-subsidised-weight-loss-drugs-advocates-say",
      "description": "<p>With GLP-1s to treat the condition not specifically approved by the TGA, patients are being prescribed them off-label</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Women living with a chronic hormonal condition should have access to taxpayer-funded weight-loss medications, advocates say.</p><p>The Polyendrocrine Metabolic Ovarian Syndrome Association of Australia (POSAA) is urging for GLP-1 drugs to be approved on the Pharmaceutical Benefits Scheme for people living with the condition.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/10/women-with-pmos-should-get-subsidised-weight-loss-drugs-advocates-say\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-09T23:00:41"
    },
