      "description": "<p>Global sportswear brand is suing online retailer in the federal court for selling clothes featuring ‘deceptively similar’ design</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Global sportswear brand Adidas claims Australian label White Fox is trying to trade off its reputation by infringing its distinctive three-stripe trademark.</p><p>Adidas is suing the online fast-fashion retailer in the Federal Court for selling clothes with a four-stripe design, which it argues is deceptively similar to its classic design.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/09/adidas-white-fox-fashion-australia-trading-branding-sydney-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
